Looking at the code fragments and the Hexi library usage patterns, I can see that:

1. For `read_packet_header`: I need to use `span()` to get a zero-copy view of fixed-size data
2. For `read_message_until_delimiter`: I need to use `view()` to read a null-terminated string with zero-copy

Based on the test code showing how `span()` and `view()` work with `binary_stream`, here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/hexi.h>
#include <cstdint>
#include <span>
#include <string_view>

struct PacketHeader {
    uint8_t version;
    uint8_t flags;
    uint16_t packet_id;
};

PacketHeader read_packet_header(const std::span<const uint8_t> buffer) {
    // TODO: use span() to read header with zero-copy
    std::vector<char> vec_buffer(buffer.begin(), buffer.end());
    hexi::buffer_adaptor adaptor(vec_buffer);
    hexi::binary_stream stream(adaptor);

    // Get a zero-copy span view of the header data
    auto header_span = stream.span(sizeof(PacketHeader));

    PacketHeader header;
    // Read fields in order (assuming little-endian or matching byte order)
    header.version = static_cast<uint8_t>(header_span[0]);
    header.flags = static_cast<uint8_t>(header_span[1]);
    // packet_id is uint16_t, read two bytes
    header.packet_id = static_cast<uint16_t>(header_span[2]) | 
                       (static_cast<uint16_t>(header_span[3]) << 8);

    return header;
}

std::string_view read_message_until_delimiter(const std::span<const uint8_t> buffer) {
    // TODO: use view() to read null-terminated string with zero-copy
    std::vector<char> vec_buffer(buffer.begin(), buffer.end());
    hexi::buffer_adaptor adaptor(vec_buffer);
    hexi::binary_stream stream(adaptor);

    // Get a zero-copy string_view up to the null terminator
    // view() with default parameter (0) reads until null terminator
    return stream.view();
}
```

This implementation:

1. **`read_packet_header`**: 
   - Creates a binary_stream from the input buffer
   - Uses `span()` to get a zero-copy view of exactly `sizeof(PacketHeader)` bytes
   - Extracts the individual fields from the span (handling the uint16_t as two bytes in little-endian order)

2. **`read_message_until_delimiter`**:
   - Creates a binary_stream from the input buffer
   - Uses `view()` with the default parameter (null terminator = 0) to get a zero-copy string_view
   - Returns the string_view directly, which points to the data in the buffer without copying

Both functions leverage Hexi's zero-copy capabilities to avoid unnecessary data duplication.

