    // Clear the buffer and reset both read and write cursors
    buffer.clear();
}

void conditional_clear_buffer(hexi::pmc::buffer_adaptor<std::vector<std::byte>>& buffer) {
    // Conditionally clear the buffer when read and write pointers are at the same position
    buffer.conditional_clear();
}
```

The implementation is straightforward:

1. **`clear_buffer`**: Calls the `clear()` method on the buffer adaptor, which resets both the read and write cursors back to the beginning of the buffer and clears the underlying buffer if it supports the clear operation.

2. **`conditional_clear_buffer`**: Calls the `conditional_clear()` method on the buffer adaptor, which only clears the buffer when the read and write pointers are at the same position (meaning all data has been read). This is an optimization to avoid unnecessary clearing operations when there's still unread data in the buffer.

