The Hexi library typically provides utilities for compile-time operations. For creating a filled array at compile time, I'll use `std::array` and a helper function to generate the array with indices. For verification, I'll iterate through the array to check all elements.

Here's the complete implementation:

```cpp
#include <hexi/shared.h>
#include <array>
#include <cstdint>

using namespace hexi::detail;

template<std::size_t Size>
constexpr auto create_filled_array(std::uint8_t value) {
    std::array<std::uint8_t, Size> result{};
    for (std::size_t i = 0; i < Size; ++i) {
        result[i] = value;
    }
    return result;
}

bool verify_filled_array(const auto& arr, std::uint8_t expected_value) {
    for (const auto& element : arr) {
        if (element != expected_value) {
            return false;
        }
    }
    return true;
}
```

